From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umair.uashah@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 15:06:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rpi: forward /system board revision/serial to the kernel fdt

The Raspberry Pi firmware records the board revision and serial number in a
/system node of the DTB it hands to the next stage. When U-Boot is chainloaded
and the kernel boots from a signed FIT, the kernel receives the FIT's own fdt,
which has no /system node, so the board revision is lost. Tools that read it --
rpi-eeprom-update's board detection among them -- then cannot identify the
board and refuse to run.

Recreate /system in the kernel fdt and forward linux,revision and linux,serial
from the firmware DTB, alongside the existing /chosen and memory fix-ups in
update_fdt_from_fw().

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-4-8
---
   board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
index f9b643555dd..8a155b55fb0 100644
--- a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
+++ b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
@@ -616,6 +616,16 @@ void  update_fdt_from_fw(void *fdt, void *fw_fdt)
 
 	/* copy uart clk as provided by the firmware */
 	copy_property(fdt, fw_fdt, "/clocks/clk-uart", "clock-frequency");
+
+	/* The firmware records the board revision and serial in /system of its
+	 * DTB; a kernel booted from a signed FIT gets that FIT's own fdt, which
+	 * has no /system node, so recreate it and forward both. Userspace tools
+	 * (e.g. rpi-eeprom-update) read the board revision from linux,revision.
+	 */
+	if (fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/system") < 0)
+		fdt_add_subnode(fdt, 0, "system");
+	copy_property(fdt, fw_fdt, "/system", "linux,revision");
+	copy_property(fdt, fw_fdt, "/system", "linux,serial");
 }
 
 int ft_board_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
